==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|netze}}, from {{inh|de|goh|nezzi}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*natją}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*ned-||to turn, twist, knot}}. Akin to Dutch {{m|nl|net}}, Low German {{m|nds|Nett}}, English {{m|en|net}}, Danish {{m|da|net}}, Swedish {{m|sv|nät}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/nɛt͡s/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Netz.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Netzes|Netze}}

# [[net]]; [[web]]; [[mesh]] {{gloss|construction of interwoven fibres, e.g. that of a fisher, a spider, etc.}}
# {{lb|de|general|also|telecommunication}} [[network]]; [[grid]] {{gloss|a system, often interconnected, that covers a certain area}}
# {{lb|de|informal|telecommunication}} [[signal]] {{gloss|connection to a network}}
# {{lb|de|informal|with definite article}} the [[internet]]

